# Engram memory and session state — local to this machine. .claude/scripts/
# are symlinks into ~/.engram, so committing them would break for anyone else.
# Remove this line if the team decides to share memory (engram itself expects
# that). CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the working agreement for
# this repo — the platform traps, the testing rules, the doctype standard and
# the delivery loop — and it is worth nothing on one laptop.
.claude/
